  "question": {
    "text": "Let the position vectors of two points <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Q</mi></math>&nbsp;be <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>-</mo><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">j</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">k</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">j</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">k</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></math>, respectively. Let&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>S</mi></math> be two points such that the direction ratios of lines <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><mi>R</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Q</mi><mi>S</mi></math> are <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>, respectively. Let lines <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><mi>R</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Q</mi><mi>S</mi></math> intersect at&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>T</mi></math>. If the vector <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mover><mrow><mi>T</mi><mi>A</mi></mrow><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover></math> is perpendicular to both <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mover><mrow><mi>P</mi><mi>R</mi></mrow><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mover><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mi>S</mi></mrow><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover></math> and the length of vector <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mover><mrow><mi>T</mi><mi>A</mi></mrow><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover></math>&nbsp;is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msqrt><mn>5</mn></msqrt></math> units, then the modulus of a position vector of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math> is :",
